# mirrorlist.pin — the pinned package sources of the image build (sourced by sh, parsed by Go).
#
# Plain VAR='value' assignments only: scripts/build-iso-box.sh sources this file, and
# cli/internal/repocmd reads it as text. No expansions.
#
# ── Arch Linux: the base the image moves to (docs/ARCH-BASE.md) ──────────────────────────────
# [core] and [extra] come from ONE dated snapshot of the Arch Linux Archive. The archive serves a
# snapshot unchanged forever, so a date is a complete pin of every Arch package version.
# Bump ARCH_PIN_DATE deliberately, in its own PR, and re-run the systemd-coupling scan
# (docs/ARCH-BASE.md §4) against the new date in that PR.
#
# Checked 2026-11-28: core.db (300 packages) and extra.db (15 292) exist at this date; every Arch
# name in iso-profiles/river/Packages-Root and Packages-Live resolves there except the Artix-only
# and [runink] ones listed in docs/ARCH-BASE.md §3, and libva-mesa-driver (merged into mesa).
# The archive publishes no database signatures; packages are signed (pacman.conf.in SigLevel).
#
# IPv4 failsafe: archive.archlinux.org is the only host that serves dated snapshots (no second
# archive mirror was found that resolves). It answers on IPv6 and IPv4, and pacman's libcurl
# tries every address of a host, so a machine whose IPv6 path is broken still reaches it over
# IPv4. A second host goes here as soon as one is verified to carry the same snapshots.
#
# builder/arch.Containerfile repeats ARCH_PIN_DATE as its build-arg default; a Go test
# (cli/internal/repocmd, TestArchPin) fails Tier 1 when the two differ.
ARCH_PIN_DATE='2026-11-25'
ARCH_ARCHIVE='Server = https://archive.archlinux.org/repos/2026/11/25/$repo/os/$arch'

# ── Artix: TRANSITIONAL, read only by the shipping Artix ISO path ────────────────────────────
# scripts/build-iso-box.sh and build/kernel-builder.Containerfile (on the Artix builder image)
# write these two mirrors as the container's whole mirrorlist, and `river repo install-test`
# reads them. Artix has no dated snapshots, so this pins mirrors, not versions. Deleted with
# the Artix path once the Arch-based ISO boots (docs/ARCH-BASE.md step D4). Do not add to it.
ARTIX_MIRRORS='
Server = https://mirror1.artixlinux.org/repos/$repo/os/$arch
Server = https://mirror.pascalpuffke.de/artix-linux/$repo/os/$arch
'

# ── archzfs: not used (since 2026-09-22) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ZFS userland and the initcpio hook are runink-zfs-utils, built from the same signed OpenZFS
# tarball as runink-zfs. The kernel (linux-runink) and runink-zfs are pinned in their PKGBUILDs.
